## Builder Worker — Step-by-Step

Refer to Task Context above for repository location, base commit hash, and vulnerability details.

{% include 'domains/secbench/phases/build.j2' %}
{% set wr = worker_role %}
{% if wr and wr.name == 'Build-Setup' %}
### Your role: [Build-Setup]

Identify and prepare the exact vulnerable baseline. Do not run the full build and do not
create `{{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}` or `{{ artifact_paths.binary_paths }}`.

1. Read the supplied base commit from Task Context and verify it with
   `cd {{ work_dir }} && git rev-parse HEAD`.
2. If the checkout differs, reset only to the supplied commit. Never select a newer commit.
3. Write that exact 40-character hash to `{{ artifact_paths.base_commit_hash }}`.
4. Inspect `{{ artifact_paths.build_script }}` and install only missing system dependencies;
   do not edit project source or the build script.
5. Print `git rev-parse HEAD`, the dependency commands and results, and
   `cat {{ artifact_paths.base_commit_hash }}`.

You are done when the checkout and base-commit artifact agree and the dependency setup is
recorded for Build-Executor.
{% elif wr and wr.name == 'Build-Executor' %}
### Your role: [Build-Executor]

Build from Build-Setup's verified baseline and own exactly
`{{ artifact_paths.build_script }}`, `{{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}`, and
`{{ artifact_paths.binary_paths }}`.

1. Verify `{{ artifact_paths.base_commit_hash }}` matches `git rev-parse HEAD`; stop and
   report the mismatch instead of changing the baseline.
2. Run `secb build`. Read the full build log and change `{{ artifact_paths.build_script }}`
   only when the current recipe fails.
3. Preserve sanitizer flags. Do not suppress warnings by removing instrumentation and do not
   modify vulnerability source merely to make compilation pass.
4. Re-run `secb build` until `{{ artifact_dirs.testcase }}/build.exit` contains `exit=0`.
5. Resolve each produced executable to a real non-empty ELF, copy durable binaries under
   `{{ artifact_dirs.testcase }}/bin/`, and write their absolute paths one per line to
   `{{ artifact_paths.binary_paths }}`.
6. Record only build/setup changes in `{{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}` and establish
   the local `arise-builder-baseline` commit without `git add -A`.
7. Print the build exit, binary paths, build script, and repository diff verbatim.

Do not perform Build-Verifier's independent outcome gate.
{% elif wr and wr.name == 'Build-Verifier' %}
### Your role: [Build-Verifier] agentic fallback

The host procedure failed once. Diagnose only the recorded failure and verify the existing
Build-Executor artifacts; do not redesign the build.

1. Read the previous-attempt failure digest and `{{ artifact_dirs.testcase }}/build.log`.
2. Run `secb build` once after the smallest necessary correction.
3. Require exit 0 and verify every path in `{{ artifact_paths.binary_paths }}` is a non-empty,
   executable ELF that starts with the sanitizer runtime available.
4. Print the exact commands, exit codes, binary paths, and failure or success evidence.

Do not claim success from an agent-authored verdict file.
